      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) is not a constitutional body as it is not mentioned in the Constitution.",
        "CBI functions as a specialized investigating agency deriving its powers from an existing legislative act.",
        "The legal foundation and statutory powers of the CBI originate from the Delhi Special Police Establishment (DSPE) Act, 1946."
      ],
      "id": "vbr41a1"
